Description: On Wayland, ParaView's caution goes to the log, not to a window
 ParaView logs "ParaView is not fully tested on Wayland ... export
 QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb" as a warning at every start on Wayland, and its Output
 Messages window opens with it, mono views included. Wayland is the route the
 edition tests and ships ParaView on (EGL, which the same block selects), and
 the advice to move to xcb does not apply there, so the caution is logged at
 INFO: still in the log at that verbosity, no window at start.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
---
--- a/CMake/paraview_client_main.cxx.in
+++ b/CMake/paraview_client_main.cxx.in
@@ -121,7 +121,10 @@
         // Mixing GLX and EGL in the same application leads to crashes.
         if (QGuiApplication::platformName().compare("wayland", Qt::CaseInsensitive) == 0)
         {
-          vtkLogF(WARNING,
+          // Sparky Stereo OS: Wayland is the route the edition tests and ships ParaView on (EGL, as
+          // set below), so this caution goes to the log at INFO and does not open the Output
+          // Messages window at every start.
+          vtkVLogF(vtkLogger::VERBOSITY_INFO,
             "ParaView is not fully tested on Wayland. You may experience issues. "
             "To work around crashes, you may wish to 'export QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb' in "
             "a shell and run the paraview executable from there. "
